Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: A Calendar Sheds Its Skin
- Story & Context: Near the salt flats of Bilma, Kaelen dropped his only copy of the navigation logs into a chasm, hearing the paper rattle like dry leaves against the canyon floor, marking the moment our caravan lost its heading. "The numbers are weeping, drifting toward the lightless edge of the map," we whispered as the bass pulse finally stabilized into a rhythm that matched the stars.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A desolate, wind-scoured salt flat at sunset with a thousand glowing, floating digital dates dissolving into embers; vibrant, ethereal, surrealist photography.

Track 2: The Gearbox Confession
- Story & Context: Zuri stood before the smoking remnants of the main oscillator, admitting to the Council that she had fed the TR-808 stolen spice-oil instead of coolant just to hear it scream in a higher pitch. The smell of burning rubber and ozone filled the tent, yet the sound was pure gold, a "mechanical prayer rising to a god of copper and rust" that silenced our collective panic.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Close-up of a weathered, metal-clad human hand adjusting a scorched, ancient 808 knob with sparks flying; intricate details, cyberpunk-nomad aesthetic, macro lens, cinematic depth of field.

Track 3: 04:15 – Appointment at the Singularity
- Story & Context: Legend says that if you stand at the Oasis of Zero at exactly the wrong hour, the ghost of the lead mechanic appears to trade a perfectly tuned frequency for your sense of time, leaving you wandering the dunes forever. We heard the rhythm change in the distance, a "thud that undoes the future," and we knew we would never make it back to the city for our scheduled meetings.
